{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1405447-the-beast-made-me-do-it-a-convenient-excuse","id":1405447,"title":"The Beast made me do it! A convenient excuse?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Vampire: The Masquerade"],"posts":[{"date":"2020-07-30T19:02:08-07:00","id":1405447,"title":"The Beast made me do it! A convenient excuse?","content":"So, the more I have been playing and diving deeper into the books, lore and story of VTM. The more I notice that a huge part of the being a vampire has to do with struggling with the Beast inside them.<br /> <br /> Be it paths, humanity, or disciplines and frenzy, there is a lot of matters that are tied to the beast. If I take a drink for each time the word Beast appear in the books, I would be drunk after almost every chapter.<br /> <br /> As I read on however, I feel the Beast feels more and more like a convent plot device. Your character did anything bad? Oh no, it's not that you are playing a bad person, it's cos the beast made your character did it. Going on a blood drench frenzy? That just the beast's primal survival instincts. Diablerizing another kindred? The beast demands it. Sabbat being who they are? It's not their fault! It's cos they love the beast. And so forth. <br /> <br /> Blame not thy self, blame the Beast. <br /> <br /> It reaches a point where... I feel unlike other TRPGs where you are kinda responsible for your character. Here players got a convent excuse whenever and however their characters does something bad.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26067-wingstorm","name":"Wingstorm","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"50"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-30T22:10:23-07:00","id":1405467,"title":"","content":"Its convenient until the neonate gets a teacher. If they aren't fully aware of anything they can blame their actions on some baser desire that takes them over.<br /> <br /> However, once they are picked up by the local vampires and taught about the new way of unlife, that excuse goes out the window. They know better now.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23908-kael03","name":"Kael03","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"230"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-30T23:17:48-07:00","id":1405480,"title":"","content":"Using this line is an express route to low humanity and being put down by whatever authorities are in the area. <br /> <br /> It's a deliberate trap. Such an easy excuse. But leaning on it means that the character isn't taking responsibility. Every time they do it, the Beast will get stronger, and their life expectancy goes down...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Prone to being a Classic Curmudgeon, goshdarned whippersnappers...","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1037-jamiemalk","name":"jamiemalk","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1037_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"399"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-31T00:46:12-07:00","id":1405495,"title":"","content":"I don't think I've ever seen the Beast be a valid excuse in any of the VtM material. Even when the Beast literally did do it, it's the vampire's failure of self-control that's presented at fault.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12892-kammerer","name":"Kammerer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12892_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1191"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-31T00:57:30-07:00","id":1405502,"title":"","content":"it is your responsibility to keep your beast in check and a kindred that fails at it is a danger to himself, the kine, other kindred and the masquarade so using that excuse is a good way to end up dragged out into the sun (on top of the degradation of your humanity as others have pointed out.) also the beast isn't a separate entity to you which you just share a body with, it's part of you.( like your conscience or your instincts)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":25992,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25992-archderd","user":"archderd","date":". 07-31-2020, 04:01 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25992-archderd","name":"archderd","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25992_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-31T02:18:27-07:00","id":1405529,"title":"","content":"Which edition are you reading?<br /> <br /> In V5, yeah, the beast has an influence in your every action, so you can always agentic shift away from what you did. Tried to escape someone's moderately unfriendly grip and ripped a guy's arm off? Beast. Got really weird in an argument? Beast. The Beast is always there and there's nothing you can do about it.<br /> <br /> <br /> In literally every other edition, this is not the case. You may feel the beast stir at times, but it doesn't seize control of your actions quite so readily. The Beast is like hunger, and it sometimes tries to possess you if it feels you're not doing a good enough job of keeping it happy. It will take control only when it feels you are threatened either by hunger or by danger or someone's attempts to provoke anger. If you play smart, you can go for very long periods without the Beast rearing it's ugly head. If the beast takes control in these editions, you deserve the blame, because you could have set your stage better.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-31T05:05:44-07:00","id":1405548,"title":"","content":"As said. &quot;In game&quot; it's a very problematic excuse because a vampire who does not control it's Beast it's a danger to everyone. If your character did something bad, it may well be better to say you did what you wanted to do (even if it actually was the Beast), otherwise you would be admitting a dangerous lack of self-control.<br /> <br /> Out of game, you know when the Beast made you do it because there's a mechanic, and you literally lose control of your character. It's almost never convinient, and hardly an excuse. If anything, it's the STs excuse to ruin your PC's day","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1683,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","user":"Aleph","date":". 07-31-2020, 08:12 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-31T08:02:54-07:00","id":1405578,"title":"","content":"This is even a bigger problem in Wraith, as the Beast is a non-Sapient entity that is controlled by the GM.<br /> <br /> The Shadow is fully aware, able to talk and reason, and is suppose to be played by fellow players, and can do much more nasty shit, then run away or kill a bunch of people.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23952-konradleijon","name":"Konradleijon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23952_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1441"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-31T08:05:17-07:00","id":1405579,"title":"","content":"You can't blame the beast for you eating a whole birthday cake (person) when you walked into the bakery (nightclub) when you are all sorts of hangry.<br /> <br /> There is a reason why the paths book is called Chaining the Beast. It's for people too weak to control their own urges so they have to find alternatives","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3953,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3953-dwight","user":"Dwight","date":". 07-31-2020, 11:07 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3953-dwight","name":"Dwight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3953_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2355"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-31T08:09:24-07:00","id":1405580,"title":"","content":"This is talked about in the \u201cDevil Advocate\u201d by Trevors chase in the shadow guide book.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23952-konradleijon","name":"Konradleijon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23952_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1441"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-31T08:12:30-07:00","id":1405582,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Konradleijon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1405447-the-beast-made-me-do-it-a-convenient-excuse?p=1405580#post1405580\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This is talked about in the \u201cDevil Advocate\u201d by Trevors chase in the shadow guide book.</div> </div> </div> </div>You should look at avatars in Mage sometime.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3953-dwight","name":"Dwight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3953_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2355"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-31T08:22:08-07:00","id":1405584,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://www.reddit.com/r/CrossoverIdeas/comments/i1945r/devils_advacote_by_trevor_chase/\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.reddit.com/r/CrossoverId..._trevor_chase/</a> Here it is.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23952-konradleijon","name":"Konradleijon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23952_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1441"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-31T09:48:12-07:00","id":1405596,"title":"","content":"I don't know if it's an &quot;excuse&quot; so much as a reason. You struggle with urges more intense than the human mind was designed for, and so you routinely lose. The result is a bit like &quot;American Werewolf In London&quot;. You technically aren't responsible for individual actions, but are responsible, to put it bluntly, for not killing yourself. You know perfectly well that you are going to kill again, and that you can't stop yourself from periodically killing. And every dawn when you crawl into your box instead of watching the sunrise, you make yourself indirectly responsible for all of those actions that you won't be able to control directly.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3598-cajunkhan","name":"CajunKhan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3598_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1700"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-31T09:56:25-07:00","id":1405602,"title":"","content":"I disagree. Giving into your Beast all the time does make your character a bad person.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-31T10:01:14-07:00","id":1405605,"title":"","content":"It's not &quot;giving in&quot;. The urges are literally too strong to beat consistently. That's what is represented not only by frenzies, but by various beastial results.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3598-cajunkhan","name":"CajunKhan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3598_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1700"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-31T15:55:38-07:00","id":1405682,"title":"","content":"I do think vampires disassociate when they call their new urges &quot;the beast&quot; and speak of it as separate from them. I suppose it is a natural coping mechanism. But to me, the newly embraced vampire ends up with an entirely new set of emotional responses which is completely alien to the previously human mindset. So it is a natural reaction to brand it as &quot;other&quot;, and &quot;not me&quot;.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2471-trollroot","name":"Trollroot","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"311"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-31T17:52:44-07:00","id":1405707,"title":"","content":"The beast made me do it is only an excuse (more accurately a weak excuse) to my mind when you use it to gloss over the mistakes the beast <i>didn't</i> force you to make, such as going hunting in a stressful situation with high hunger being a mistake that enabled the beast to have an advantage over you and take it. Of course the beast is the one that drained that mortal dry, but that doesn't absolve you of the fact that you put yourself in a situation where that was a not insignificant risk. On the flip side the beast is in fact a tangible, detectable, manipulable entity that can be drawn to the fore or pushed aside with sufficient disciplines.That to me means it is not only definitely a thing and definitely an excuse at times, but also something other vampires would be forced to acknowledge as a thing too. I mean it's hard to deny the beast exists when you have an Animalism power to detect it and others to make it do things. I suppose some might call it by different names and have different theories for it across sects and backgrounds and clans, but really I think it's been enough of a constant aspect of vampiric existence that it's likely codified and understood well enough.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12093-pixelpuzzler","name":"PixelPuzzler","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"80"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-01T02:42:54-07:00","id":1405769,"title":"","content":"I thought the Beast was just a metaphorical construct. Or is that in Requiem?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-01T02:43:33-07:00","id":1405770,"title":"","content":"A metaphor for a vampire\u2019s predatory urges.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-01T02:52:51-07:00","id":1405772,"title":"","content":"How did you...<br /> <br /> No it's an actual entity that resides in the body of a vampire.<br /> <br /> Pre-V5, it's an entity that possesses you when you screw up<br /> <br /> V5, it's an entity that possesses you so that you screw up.<br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:8px\">There are various powers that take advantage of it, including one where you can give it to other people. </span>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":25794,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","user":"MyWifeIsScary","date":". 08-01-2020, 05:55 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-01T05:35:22-07:00","id":1405781,"title":"","content":"the beast isn't exclusive to vampires, <br /> the beast is in every being, <br /> it's just wilder in vampires<br /> <br /> the beast is the seat of your passion, <br /> it's what allows you to stand up and want to do things, have a party, yelling to cheer for your favorite team, beat someone up, or take revenge on someone<br /> <br /> without it, you're hardly better than a walking vegetable <br /> <br /> animalism 3, for example, used to be about shutting down the beast of a mortal to pacify them or render them helpless","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>-</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10998-pleiades","name":"Pleiades","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10998_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1844"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-01T05:44:50-07:00","id":1405783,"title":"","content":"It\u2019s a persons Id? In Freudian terms?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23952-konradleijon","name":"Konradleijon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23952_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1441"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-01T08:53:47-07:00","id":1405798,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Pleiades</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1405447-the-beast-made-me-do-it-a-convenient-excuse?p=1405781#post1405781\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">the beast isn't exclusive to vampires,<br /> the beast is in every being,<br /> it's just wilder in vampires<br /> <br /> the beast is the seat of your passion,<br /> it's what allows you to stand up and want to do things, have a party, yelling to cheer for your favorite team, beat someone up, or take revenge on someone<br /> <br /> without it, you're hardly better than a walking vegetable<br /> <br /> animalism 3, for example, used to be about shutting down the beast of a mortal to pacify them or render them helpless</div> </div> </div> </div>This is correct. And this is true in V5 as well:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong> Sense the Beast V5 Animalism 1 dot power</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">The vampire can sense the Beast present in <b>mortals</b>, vampires, and other supernaturals, gaining a sense of their nature, hunger, and hostility.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong> Quell the Beast V5 Animalism 3 dot power</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">By locking eyes with a target, the vampire cows their inner Beast into temporary slumber. <b>Mortals</b> affected thus become apathetic, unable to take any actions other than to stay alive, while vampires\u2019 bestial urges temporarily abate, for better or worse.</div> </div> </div> </div>The Beast is the most primal part of human nature. The difference with Vampires is their Beast is often unchained and much stronger than the one residing into human souls.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24992-haquim","name":"Haquim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24992_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-01T09:21:21-07:00","id":1405799,"title":"","content":"No, no, no. Stop the Toreador poetry, you're just confusing people. <br /> <br /> in Vtm the beast isn't your Id on steroids. It's a spirit that takes route in the heart of every vampire. It's a foreign entity that comes with the blood. you could hypothesize the beast is just a grossly mutated aspect of someone's sleeping avatar, or if it's a foreign entity that has fed off you to mold itself; at the end of the day, it's not a fucking metaphore; it's not your character's pent up desires. It's not your first mate that helps you acheive your goals with a firm hand, it's a mutinous high jacker that's looking for an excuse to take the boat.<br /> <br /> <br /> From a meta perspective, sure you can say it is your id. That's poetic, sure. but your character would be a fool to go along with that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":25794,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","user":"MyWifeIsScary","date":". 08-01-2020, 12:23 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-01T10:43:36-07:00","id":1405808,"title":"","content":"There seems to be a huge divide on this issue. And it doesn\u2019t help that there are two games about vampires and the vampires in both games have Beasts but the Beasts are different so people who aren\u2019t like super familiar with the details of both games might get the two Beasts confused.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-01T10:44:57-07:00","id":1405809,"title":"","content":"I\u2019m more familiar with Masquerade but sometimes I get the rules confused. Like I know Predator\u2019s Taint is Requiem but sometimes I forget the details.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-01T11:08:09-07:00","id":1405814,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1405447-the-beast-made-me-do-it-a-convenient-excuse?p=1405799#post1405799\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">at the end of the day, it's not a fucking metaphore; it's not your character's pent up desires. It's not your first mate that helps you acheive your goals with a firm hand,</div> </div> </div> </div>yes, it isn't a metaphore, the beast is a real thing<br /> <br /> but no, it is an integral part of your personality and your ability to function,<br /> devoid of a beast, a human or a vampire are just smart vegetables<br /> <br /> this isn't poetry, it's canon, v20 canon, and revised canon (and apparently v5 as well)<br /> in the description of v20 animalism 5:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> If the character leaves the target\u2019s presence before<br /> the frenzy expends itself, the vampire loses his Beast,<br /> perhaps permanently. While no longer vulnerable to<br /> frenzy, the character cannot use or regain Willpower<br /> and becomes increasingly lethargic. To recover the<br /> Beast, he must find the person who now possesses it<br /> (who likely isn\u2019t enjoying herself very much) and coax<br /> the Beast into its proper vessel. The most effective way<br /> to do so is to behave in ways that make the Beast want<br /> to return \u2014 however, this isn\u2019t a guarantee that it will<br /> wish to do so. Alternatively, the character can simply<br /> kill the host (thus causing the Beast to return to the<br /> vampire immediately). </div> </div> </div>as for the beast being a foreign entity or not is unclear,<br /> I'd say it is foreign, the beast-of-war from garou myth,<br /> but it remains nonetheless important to any being...unless you fancy the vegetable life (no offense to any vegetables reading this)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>-</b>","edited":{"userid":10998,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10998-pleiades","user":"Pleiades","date":". 08-01-2020, 02:23 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10998-pleiades","name":"Pleiades","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10998_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1844"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-01T11:45:57-07:00","id":1405816,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1405447-the-beast-made-me-do-it-a-convenient-excuse?p=1405799#post1405799\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">No, no, no. Stop the Toreador poetry, you're just confusing people.<br /> <br /> in Vtm the beast isn't your Id on steroids. It's a spirit that takes route in the heart of every vampire. It's a foreign entity that comes with the blood. you could hypothesize the beast is just a grossly mutated aspect of someone's sleeping avatar, or if it's a foreign entity that has fed off you to mold itself; at the end of the day, it's not a fucking metaphore; it's not your character's pent up desires. It's not your first mate that helps you acheive your goals with a firm hand, it's a mutinous high jacker that's looking for an excuse to take the boat.<br /> <br /> <br /> From a meta perspective, sure you can say it is your id. That's poetic, sure. but your character would be a fool to go along with that.</div> </div> </div> </div>Everyone has a Beast, every mortal has a Beast (which is why vampires can sense and manipulate the Beasts of mortals) Every vampire had a Beast before they were a vampire, back when they were mortal, because mortals have Beasts. So it is a natural condition to humans (insofar as every human having a monstreous creature attached to their soul is natural) and a natural condition to vampires. It's just that the Beast is usually silent and slumbering in mortals but it's awake and active in vampires.<br /> <br /> Due to the Christian perspective of VtM one could perhaps make links between the Beast and sin with the idea that everyone possess Original Sin (the Beast), but Vampires, due to their existence beyond God's forgiveness have a much more powerful and active Beast.<br /> <br /> More on topic, every vampire has to keep a tight lock on their Beast. Those who fail to do so end up turning into wrights, insane ravening monsters who need to be put down. While a vampire could &quot;blame their beast&quot; for something they do in frenzy, that's not really a &quot;get out of jail free&quot; card because it shows that the vampire lacks the power to control their Beast and is at danger of eventually becoming a wright. People might look the other way once, but a vampire who gives into Frenzy and the Beast too often is going to very quickly start facing serious repercussions.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":741,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","user":"AnubisXy","date":". 08-02-2020, 01:33 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-02T18:40:13-07:00","id":1406031,"title":"","content":"The way I see, vampire powers often work in a very metaphorical way, so vampires being able to manipulate the beast doesn't prove it's a separate creature anymore than vampires getting bonuses from humors proves the middle-ages humor theories to be scientifically correct.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3598-cajunkhan","name":"CajunKhan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3598_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1700"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-02T20:42:13-07:00","id":1406049,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Penelope</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1405447-the-beast-made-me-do-it-a-convenient-excuse?p=1405769#post1405769\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I thought the Beast was just a metaphorical construct. Or is that in Requiem?</div> </div> </div> </div>That's Requiem.<br /> <br /> In Masquerade, the Beast is a specific, individual entity that's fuelled by your base desires and above all else loves to fuck you over. It theoretically wants to get blood and avoid fire, but it's often worse at that than you are. The big theme is <i>loss of control</i>; if the Beast takes over, it's almost exclusively a bad thing that will hurt you, so you need to keep it contained or find ways to negotiate with it (such as Instinct paths) or else it'll ruin everything.<br /> <br /> In Requiem, the Beast is an individual entity the same way Freud's <i>id</i> or Jung's &quot;shadow&quot; is an individual entity: it's a useful name to give to a part of your own mind, but it's not actually an alien influence in your head. It's part of you, it wants what you want, and it's willing to do anything to get that thing. (It's also what fuels disciplines.) The big theme is <i>the price of power</i>; the Beast pushes you to get what you want and not let anything stand in your way, and doesn't care how much blood ends up on your hands.<br /> <br /> (This is the take that's supported by most of the books, at least. Different editions muddy the waters to various extents. But the thematics stay the same.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24808-draconis","name":"Draconis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24808_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"805"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-03T00:06:07-07:00","id":1406072,"title":"","content":"Yeah , I like the Requiem version better, the Beast being your Id instead of a alien influence makes it feel more like it\u2019s your fault if you frenzy.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23952-konradleijon","name":"Konradleijon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23952_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1441"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-03T01:41:30-07:00","id":1406079,"title":"","content":"The requiem idea sounds fine. I haven't played, so i can't say much<br /> I really liked the way VTM used to do it. <br /> <br /> The V5 system is really the worst of both worlds; Too alien to really be you like in VTR. Too omnipressent to really be something you can strive to control like in VTM (not to mention this combination really strains on the masquerade more than other editions)<br /> If they had kept VTM's heast as it it would have been better, if they went full VTR (I'm sure there would have been complaints) it would have been better. But... they did what they did, and it works for less people .","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-03T05:26:10-07:00","id":1406094,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24808-draconis\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar24808_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"24808\" data-vbnamecard=\"24808\">Draconis</a> thanks \ud83d\ude0a. I always got the two confused, but now I\u2019ve got them straight.<br /> <br /> I like the Masquerade setting, but I like Requiem\u2019s Beast a lot better. I\u2019d probably merge the two if I ever ran a game.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-03T05:27:28-07:00","id":1406096,"title":"","content":"I would use Requiem\u2019s Beast in the Masquerade (V5) setting.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]}]}